// `x && y` reads as `x & &y`. On integers that was a bit and, so a logical
// and written the C way compiled to a different answer. A borrow is not an
// operand of `&`, and the diagnostic names the spelling Kizu uses.
fn main() {
    let x = 6;
    let y = 3;
    print(x && y);
    return;
}

// check-fails
// features: bitwise diagnostics
// error: `&&` is not an operator; logical and is written `and`
